  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 327 AM EDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nHigh pressure continues to build in over the course of the long \nterm, limiting the chances of afternoon thunderstorms while slowly \nincreasing afternoon high temps and with it heat indices. Temps will \nreturn to the mid 90s by the middle of the week with widespread \ntriple digit heat index values along and south of I-85. A heat \nadvisory may be needed for the southern portions of the CWA as early \nas Monday. \n\nOvernight lows will also be on the rise with the return of the mid \n70s to much of the area. This doesn't do much in providing relief \nfrom the daytime heat; especially for vulnerable populations. Look \nafter each other, and keep an eye on pets and kids. Stay hydrated if \nyou plan to spend time outside.\n\nThunderstorm chances during the afternoon will be down to less than \n10% for much of the area through the week. As a result, the chances \nof cooling off with an afternoon thunderstorm decrease with it.",
